<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 15.49 µm on Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis18 (428.3 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "critical_k, sigma_of_k and the diffusivity solver are named for the Turing wavenumber. Lean theorems encode the same trace, determinant, diffusion numerator and the 5 < 11 < 14 mode ordering. The cubic closure is only briefly identified." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 15.49 µm on Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis18 (428.3 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The script solves k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v) / (2 D_u D_v) for lambda_c = 15.49 µm and checks trace < 0, det > 0, and the diffusion-ratio numerator. Euler integration of the Fourier symbol tracks the analytical growth rate (r = 0.9948). Cubic saturation is a closure, not Schnakenberg's full mass-action system." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 15.49 µm on Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis18 (428.3 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Rib-span fraction on the pinned photograph is 0.2245. The 16-mode fit to that span has Pearson r = 0.9832, RMSE = 0.182 and KS D = 0.035, none equal to its reference. Specimen coherency and circularity are measured and differ from the reference baselines. The fit is still one in-sample transect." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-diffusivity-sweep-pearson-r-of-lambda-c-versus-sqrt-alpha>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-dispersion-curve-pearson-r-analytical-k-vs-explicit-euler>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-equal-diffusion-ablation-max-re-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-holaspis18-repeats-of-15-49-m-along-one-thoracic-pitch>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-contour-circularity>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-ks-statistic-between-axial-rib-profile-and-16-mode-reconstruction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-rib-train-pearson-r-16-mode-turing-truncation-vs-axial-profile>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-image-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 15.49 µm on Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis18 (428.3 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 85.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Linear Turing wavelength is solved so lambda_c = 15.49 µm at D_v/D_u = 40 with the holaspis18 Jacobian (trace -0.56 s^-1, det > 0). Explicit Euler matches the analytical dispersion at Pearson r = 0.9948. Equal diffusion is a negative control (max Re sigma = -0.048 s^-1). Repeats of that wavelength per thoracic pitch are 5 (meraspis, 428.5 Ma), 11 (this 18-segment holaspid, 428.3 Ma) and 14 (holaspis22, 428.1 Ma). The 14 mm Commons photograph's rib span gives an in-sample 16-mode Pearson r = 0.9832. The growth GIF is 12 frames at 720×540. The cuticle carrier is still painted inside a geometric oval rather than a segmented outline. Overall 85.3/100 (faithfulness 84.7, reproducibility 86.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 82, Parameter expressivity 86, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 86. Output judged: docs/media/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis18_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d14afcec6c366e1b9274a6586a0de48fc, image/png, 979071 B, 1248×960 px, artifact_sha256 22224bf0abc520238f1fb610f0595ebeabc0ff3b332fc8a8947374144686c8cd (sha256 22224bf0abc520238f1fb610f0595ebeabc0ff3b332fc8a8947374144686c8cd), spec_fingerprint a8d8d68eaa2ce087b7e2a7e143f02ff889326157548ffa190bc5cdb91f8c1ad9. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: a8d8d68eaa2ce087b7e2a7e143f02ff889326157548ffa190bc5cdb91f8c1ad9; artifact_sha256: 22224bf0abc520238f1fb610f0595ebeabc0ff3b332fc8a8947374144686c8cd; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis18_turing_wavelength_s0/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis18_specimen.jpg=50ac5dbca8261978..., datasets/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis18_turing_wavelength_s0/aulacopleura_koninckii_holaspis18_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=e33257c717547148...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hughes & Chapman 1995 and Fusco et al. 2004: Aulacopleura konincki adds thoracic segments through the meraspid period and holaspids vary in segment number, including an 18-segment morphotype. | Fusco, Hong & Hughes 2016: axial growth gradients make trunk pitch non-uniform. | Turing 1952: a reaction-diffusion instability selects a finite critical wavelength. | Commons File:Aulacopleura konincki.jpg is a 14 mm Silurian specimen, CC BY-SA 3.0.; reconstructed_in_script: Jacobian entries, diffusion ratio 40, and D_u solved so lambda_c = 15.49 µm (1.549e-05 m) at 428.3 Ma. | Rib-span fraction 0.2245 measured on the pinned photograph and applied to the 4.2 mm meraspis and 22 mm holaspis22 characteristic lengths. | Mode counts 5, 11 and 14 repeats of 15.49 µm per pitch. | Sixteen-mode Fourier fit to the photograph's axial rib profile (Pearson r = 0.9832).; transfer_boundary: The species_gallery meraspis, holaspis18 and holaspis22 JPEGs are byte-identical, so predecessor and successor pitches are not re-measured on separate fossils. | The 15 µm carrier is painted at the photograph's resolved rib wavenumber; the photograph does not resolve a 15 µm lattice.; does_not_claim: Does not claim a measured holochroal lens diameter of 15.49 µm for this species. | Does not claim the geometric oval is a segmented cuticle outline. | Does not claim an independent second assessor.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [independent_assessor/model-fidelity, pressure P=1.3]: Single builder-assessor. A second model has not scored this script.",
        "open need [morphometric_validation/morphometric-validation, pressure P=1.5]: Score a second lateral transect of the rib train; the 16-mode Pearson r is still in-sample on one band.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/specimen-match, pressure P=1.7]: Replace the geometric oval with a Sobel cuticle mask and recompute cv_sim_similarity.",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R1', 'item': 'Replace the geometric oval mask with a Sobel cuticle mask and recompute image CV similarity.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R2', 'item': 'Add a second lateral transect so the rib-train Pearson r is not only in-sample on one axial band.'}",
        "remediation needed: {'id': 'R3', 'item': 'Independent second assessor (different model) — still builder-scored.'}" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.53e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Turing wavenumber at 15.49 µm on Aulacopleura koninckii holaspis18 (428.3 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Multiplying both diffusivities by alpha in {0.25, 0.5, 1, 2, 4} moves lambda_c monotonically as 15.49*sqrt(alpha) (Pearson r > 0.98). Setting D_v = D_u closes the Turing band (max Re sigma < 0). Segment count changes N at fixed k_c across the chronoseries." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-aulacopleura-koninckii-holaspis18-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

